usrsock: pass MSG_DONTWAIT to the daemon; let it end a waiting send with -EAGAIN

Purpose: the NINA socket driver (nuttx/drivers/nina, CONFIG_NET_USRSOCK_CUSTOM)
ports the Zephyr build's NINA socket offload (drivers/nina/nina_socket.c),
whose send and receive calls behave differently when the call does not wait
and whose waiting TCP send gives up with EAGAIN after 10 s.

- usrsock_sendmsg() and usrsock_recvmsg() cleared MSG_DONTWAIT before the
  request, so the daemon could not tell whether the call waits, and the
  next pass of their loop (after the daemon answered -EAGAIN) waited even
  for a call made with MSG_DONTWAIT on a blocking socket.  Now the flag
  stays set, and is also set for a non-blocking socket, so the daemon sees
  it in the request's flags.
- usrsock_sendmsg() repeats a request the daemon answers -EAGAIN for as
  long as the call waits (only SO_SNDTIMEO ends that), so a daemon could
  not end a waiting send with EAGAIN.  An answer of -ETIME now ends the
  call with -EAGAIN, as an expired SO_SNDTIMEO does.

Zephyr: drivers/nina/nina_socket.c do_send() (NINA_SEND_WAIT_MS, EAGAIN
after it; EAGAIN at once with MSG_DONTWAIT or a non-blocking socket) and
udp_send() (EAGAIN at once when the module does not take the datagram).

diff --git a/net/usrsock/usrsock_recvmsg.c b/net/usrsock/usrsock_recvmsg.c
--- a/net/usrsock/usrsock_recvmsg.c
+++ b/net/usrsock/usrsock_recvmsg.c
@@ -392,9 +392,15 @@
 
       usrsock_setup_datain(conn, inbufs, nitems(inbufs));
 
-      /* MSG_DONTWAIT is only use in usrsock. */
+      /* Tell the daemon whether the call waits: MSG_DONTWAIT for a
+       * non-blocking socket too.  The flag stays set for the next pass of
+       * the loop, which must not wait either.
+       */
 
-      flags &= ~MSG_DONTWAIT;
+      if (_SS_ISNONBLOCK(conn->sconn.s_flags))
+        {
+          flags |= MSG_DONTWAIT;
+        }
 
       /* Request user-space daemon to close socket. */
 
diff --git a/net/usrsock/usrsock_sendmsg.c b/net/usrsock/usrsock_sendmsg.c
--- a/net/usrsock/usrsock_sendmsg.c
+++ b/net/usrsock/usrsock_sendmsg.c
@@ -362,9 +362,15 @@
           goto errout_unlock;
         }
 
-      /* MSG_DONTWAIT is only use in usrsock. */
+      /* Tell the daemon whether the call waits: MSG_DONTWAIT for a
+       * non-blocking socket too.  The flag stays set for the next pass of
+       * the loop, which must not wait either.
+       */
 
-       flags &= ~MSG_DONTWAIT;
+      if (_SS_ISNONBLOCK(conn->sconn.s_flags))
+        {
+          flags |= MSG_DONTWAIT;
+        }
 
       /* Request user-space daemon to close socket. */
 
@@ -378,6 +384,16 @@
         }
 
       usrsock_teardown_request_callback(&state);
+
+      /* -ETIME: the daemon gave up waiting for room itself.  Return
+       * -EAGAIN, as for an expired SO_SNDTIMEO, without trying again.
+       */
+
+      if (ret == -ETIME)
+        {
+          ret = -EAGAIN;
+          break;
+        }
     }
   while (ret == -EAGAIN);
 
